1,Massachusetts Institute of Technology (MIT),USA,"Cambridge, Massachusetts",MIT own application portal (not Common App) · Fall 2027,Early Action: 1 Nov 2026,~5 Jan 2027,Aug–Jan,,https://mitadmissions.org/apply/,75,USD,"₹6,680","64,000","67,000",USD,57,59.6,"MIT has topped the QS rankings for 15 straight years, and its undergraduate experience is built around doing, not just studying. Through UROP, most students join real research projects, often from their first year, working alongside faculty on everything from fusion energy to AI. The culture rewards building things — hackathons, maker spaces and startup programmes are part of daily life, and graduates go on to found companies at an extraordinary rate. MIT is need-blind for international applicants and meets full demonstrated need, so finances do not block admission. Its location in Cambridge, next to Harvard and the Kendall Square biotech cluster, gives students access to one of the densest innovation ecosystems in the world, with internships and research collaborations on the doorstep.",No ED; very low intl admit rate. Fee waivers available.,"MIT's mission is to advance knowledge and educate students in science, technology and other areas of scholarship that will best serve the nation and the world in the 21st century. It aims to generate, disseminate and preserve knowledge, and to work with others to bring that knowledge to bear on the world's great challenges. Central to this is the motto 'mens et manus' — mind and hand — which reflects a belief that rigorous theory should be paired with practical application. MIT commits to giving students an education that combines academic rigour with the excitement of discovery, within a diverse campus community, and to developing in each member of that community the ability and passion to work wisely, creatively and effectively for the betterment of humankind.","MIT envisions itself as a global leader whose research and teaching produce real solutions to humanity's hardest problems. Its strategic priorities focus on climate and sustainability, health and life sciences, computing and AI (through the Schwarzman College of Computing), and the responsible use of technology in society. The Institute aims to keep an excellent education accessible to the most talented students regardless of financial background, to strengthen its innovation ecosystem so discoveries move quickly into the world, and to build a more inclusive community. MIT also sees its role as national and global — partnering with industry, government and other universities to tackle challenges at a scale no single institution could address alone, while preserving a culture of open inquiry and hands-on problem-solving."
2,Imperial College London,UK,"South Kensington, London",UCAS · Sept 2027,15 Oct 2026 (Medicine only),~14 Jan 2027 (UCAS equal-consideration date),Sept–Jan,,https://www.imperial.ac.uk/study/apply/undergraduate/,28.5,GBP,"₹3,360","40,000","50,000",GBP,47.2,59,"Imperial is the UK's top-ranked university and one of only a few in the world focused entirely on science, engineering, medicine and business. That focus means every course is deeply technical and closely linked to industry and research. Students learn in South Kensington, in the heart of London's museum quarter, with easy access to the City, tech startups and leading hospitals. Imperial's integrated MEng and MSci degrees let students earn a master's in four years, and many programmes include industrial placements or year-abroad options. Graduate employability is among the best in the UK, with strong pipelines into engineering, finance, consulting and healthcare. Its Enterprise Lab and incubators actively support student startups, making it an excellent choice for applicants who want rigorous STEM training with real-world impact.",Medicine £55k+/yr. Some courses need admissions tests (e.g. ESAT).,"Imperial's mission is to achieve enduring excellence in research and education in science, engineering, medicine and business for the benefit of society. It seeks to combine fundamental discovery with practical application, ensuring that its research creates value in industry, healthcare and public policy. The College emphasises interdisciplinary collaboration across its faculties, and close partnership with hospitals, businesses and governments. Teaching is designed to develop critical, creative problem-solvers who can apply scientific thinking to complex challenges. Imperial also commits to building an inclusive, supportive community where talented people from all backgrounds can thrive, and to communicating science openly with the public so that its work benefits society as widely as possible.","Through its 'Science for Humanity' strategy, Imperial aims to be a global leader in science-based innovation that improves lives. Its priorities include tackling climate change and the transition to net zero, advancing health through engineering and medicine, building resilient and secure technologies, and harnessing AI and data science responsibly. Imperial wants to strengthen its innovation ecosystem — including its White City campus — so that research translates quickly into startups, products and policy. It also aims to deepen international partnerships, widen access for students from under-represented backgrounds, and create an environment where people collaborate across disciplines. The overarching vision is for Imperial's scientific excellence to be directed purposefully at the biggest challenges facing society."
2,Stanford University,USA,"Stanford, California (Silicon Valley)",Common App · Fall 2027,Restrictive Early Action: 1 Nov 2026,5 Jan 2027,Aug–Jan,,https://admission.stanford.edu/apply/,90,USD,"₹8,010","67,000","71,000",USD,59.6,63.2,"Stanford sits in the heart of Silicon Valley, and few universities offer such direct access to the technology and venture capital world. Students regularly intern at, collaborate with or found startups, and the university's ecosystem has produced companies such as Google, Nvidia and Instagram. Beyond tech, Stanford is excellent across humanities, medicine, sustainability and the social sciences, and its flexible curriculum lets students explore before choosing a major. The d.school popularised design thinking, and interdisciplinary programmes connect engineering with business, policy and the arts. The campus is large and residential, with year-round sunshine and outstanding sports and research facilities. For ambitious students who want to combine academic excellence with entrepreneurship and innovation, Stanford is arguably unmatched.",Need-aware for international students.,"Stanford's founding purpose, set by Leland and Jane Stanford, is to promote the public welfare by exercising an influence on behalf of humanity and civilisation. The university aims to educate students not only for personal success but to become useful citizens who contribute to society. It seeks to advance knowledge across all fields, from fundamental science to the arts, and to apply that knowledge to real problems. Stanford emphasises freedom of inquiry, academic excellence and an entrepreneurial spirit that encourages people to take risks with new ideas. It also commits to preparing students to lead thoughtful, purposeful lives, and to building a diverse, inclusive community where people learn from one another.","Stanford's long-range vision is to be a purposeful university that accelerates solutions to pressing global problems and empowers students to lead lives of impact. Major priorities include sustainability — through the Doerr School of Sustainability — human health, the ethical development of AI and technology, and strengthening democracy and civic life. The university aims to expand interdisciplinary collaboration so that engineers, scientists, social scientists and humanists work together on complex issues. It also wants to make a Stanford education more accessible, support faculty and students in taking intellectual risks, and deepen engagement with communities beyond campus. Ultimately, Stanford envisions its research and graduates shaping a better future, in Silicon Valley and around the world."
4,University of Oxford,UK,Oxford (collegiate),UCAS · Oct 2027,15 Oct 2026 (single deadline for all courses),N/A — single October deadline,Sept–Oct,,https://www.ox.ac.uk/admissions/undergraduate/applying-to-oxford,28.5,GBP,"₹3,360","35,000","62,000",GBP,41.3,73.2,"Oxford is the oldest university in the English-speaking world and consistently one of the best. Its defining feature is the tutorial system: students meet tutors in groups of one to three to discuss their work, which builds exceptional independent thinking and argument skills. Every student belongs to one of the colleges, which provide accommodation, social life, pastoral support and a close-knit community within the larger university. Oxford offers strong programmes across humanities, sciences, medicine, law and economics, including well-known combined degrees like PPE. Degrees are mostly three years, making it efficient compared with US options. Its global alumni network includes world leaders, Nobel laureates and business pioneers, and the name carries enormous weight with employers and graduate schools.",Admissions tests + interviews (Dec). Clinical medicine at top of fee range.,"Oxford's mission is to advance learning by teaching and research and its dissemination by every means. It aims to provide an outstanding education to students of exceptional ability, regardless of background, combining the personal attention of the tutorial system with the resources of a major research university. Oxford pursues research of the highest quality across the full range of disciplines and seeks to share knowledge widely through publishing, public engagement and partnerships. The University also values academic freedom, rigorous debate and intellectual independence. Through its collegiate structure, it aims to create communities where students and academics live, learn and work together, fostering both scholarship and personal growth.","Oxford's strategic vision is to lead the world in research and education in ways that benefit society on a national and global scale. Priorities include widening access and participation so that the most able students from all backgrounds can study there, investing in research that addresses challenges such as health, climate and AI, and strengthening its innovation ecosystem so discoveries reach society — as demonstrated by its role in developing a COVID-19 vaccine. Oxford aims to remain a place of free inquiry and debate, to support its people through fair and inclusive practices, and to become environmentally sustainable. It also seeks to deepen partnerships with industry, government and international institutions to amplify its global impact."
5,Harvard University,USA,"Cambridge, Massachusetts",Common App · Fall 2027,Restrictive Early Action: 1 Nov 2026,1 Jan 2027,Aug–Jan,,https://college.harvard.edu/admissions/apply,85,USD,"₹7,570","59,000","63,000",USD,52.5,56.1,"Harvard is the world's most recognisable university brand, with unrivalled resources, faculty and alumni networks. Undergraduates study through Harvard College's liberal arts model, choosing from around 50 concentrations while building a broad base across sciences, humanities and social sciences. Harvard is need-blind for international applicants and meets full demonstrated need, making it surprisingly affordable for many families. Students live in residential houses that create close communities, and the university's libraries, museums and research centres are among the largest anywhere. Located in Cambridge near Boston, Harvard offers access to biotech, finance, policy and startup opportunities. Graduates go on to lead in government, business, academia and the arts, and the network opens doors worldwide.",Tuition only — total cost of attendance ~US$85k+.,"Harvard College's mission is to educate the citizens and citizen-leaders for our society. It aims to do this through a transformative liberal arts and sciences education that expands students' intellectual, personal and civic horizons. Harvard wants students to be exposed to new ideas, new ways of understanding and new ways of knowing, while developing the habits of mind needed for lifelong learning. Beyond academics, the College emphasises residential life and extracurricular involvement as essential to education. Harvard seeks to create an environment where students from diverse backgrounds learn from one another, build character, and prepare to contribute to their communities and the world through lives of service and leadership.","Harvard envisions advancing knowledge, promoting understanding and serving society through excellence in teaching, research and public engagement. Its priorities include expanding access through generous financial aid, advancing research in areas such as climate, health, AI and quantum science, and strengthening interdisciplinary collaboration across its schools. Harvard also aims to protect academic freedom and open discourse, support a diverse and inclusive community, and reduce its environmental footprint. Its expanding Allston campus — home to engineering and innovation activity — reflects a vision of connecting research with entrepreneurship and real-world application. Through its graduates and scholarship, Harvard aims to continue shaping leadership and ideas in the US and globally."
6,University of Cambridge,UK,Cambridge (collegiate),UCAS + My Cambridge Application · Oct 2027,15 Oct 2026 (single deadline),N/A — single October deadline,Sept–Oct,,https://www.undergraduate.study.cam.ac.uk/applying,28.5,GBP,"₹3,360","28,000","70,000",GBP,33,82.6,"Cambridge consistently ranks among the world's top universities and is especially strong in mathematics, sciences, engineering and medicine — it has produced more than 100 Nobel laureates. Teaching combines lectures with small-group supervisions, where students discuss work directly with leading academics. Every student belongs to one of 31 colleges, which provide housing, meals, support and a strong sense of community. Cambridge sits at the centre of 'Silicon Fen', a thriving cluster of tech and biotech companies that offers internships and startup opportunities. Most degrees are three years, with integrated master's options in sciences and engineering. The Cambridge name carries enormous academic and professional prestige, opening doors to top employers and graduate programmes worldwide.",Admissions tests + interviews. Medicine at top of fee range.,"Cambridge's mission is to contribute to society through the pursuit of education, learning and research at the highest international levels of excellence. Its core values include freedom of thought and expression, and freedom from discrimination. The University aims to provide an exceptional education that develops students' intellectual and personal capabilities, supported by its distinctive collegiate system. It pursues research across the widest range of disciplines, from fundamental science to the humanities, and seeks to share knowledge openly. Cambridge also emphasises the importance of fostering the relationship between academic research and industry, so that discoveries benefit society, and of encouraging a questioning spirit among students and staff.","Cambridge aims to remain one of the world's leading universities, sustaining its tradition of excellence while adapting to new challenges. Its strategic priorities include addressing climate change and sustainability, advancing health and medicine, harnessing AI responsibly, and widening access so that talented students from all backgrounds can study there. The University wants to strengthen its innovation ecosystem, supporting spin-outs and partnerships that turn research into real-world impact. It also aims to build a more inclusive community, invest in its people and infrastructure, and deepen international collaboration. The vision is of a university that combines its centuries-old commitment to free inquiry with a strong sense of purpose in solving the problems of the modern world."
7,California Institute of Technology (Caltech),USA,"Pasadena, California",Common App / QuestBridge · Fall 2027,Restrictive Early Action: 1 Nov 2026,3 Jan 2027,Aug–Jan,,https://www.admissions.caltech.edu/apply,75,USD,"₹6,680","65,000","68,000",USD,57.9,60.5,"Caltech is a small, intense powerhouse of science and engineering, with only around 1,000 undergraduates and a remarkable 3:1 student-to-faculty ratio. That size means students work closely with world-leading researchers, many of whom are Nobel laureates. Caltech manages NASA's Jet Propulsion Laboratory, giving students access to space exploration projects, and research opportunities through programmes such as SURF are widespread. The core curriculum ensures every student builds deep foundations in mathematics, physics, chemistry and biology. The Honor Code creates a culture of trust, including take-home exams. Located in Pasadena near Los Angeles, Caltech is ideal for students who love fundamental science and want a rigorous, collaborative environment where research is part of everyday life.",Pure STEM; very small intake.,"Caltech's mission is to expand human knowledge and benefit society through research integrated with education. It investigates the most challenging, fundamental problems in science and technology in a singularly collegial, interdisciplinary atmosphere, while educating outstanding students to become creative members of society. Caltech deliberately stays small so that faculty and students can collaborate closely and cross disciplinary boundaries easily. It values intellectual rigour, curiosity and integrity, reflected in its Honor Code. The Institute aims to produce graduates who think deeply, solve hard problems, and contribute to science, industry and public life, while maintaining an environment where research and teaching reinforce one another.","Caltech envisions remaining a small, focused institution that has an outsized impact on science and technology. Its strategic direction emphasises pursuing high-risk, high-reward research in areas such as quantum science, neuroscience, sustainability, AI and space exploration. Caltech aims to preserve its close-knit, collaborative culture while supporting interdisciplinary initiatives that bring physicists, biologists, engineers and computer scientists together. Through JPL and partnerships with industry, it seeks to translate discovery into technologies that benefit society. The Institute also commits to widening access for talented students, supporting diversity in science and engineering, and nurturing the next generation of researchers who will push the frontiers of knowledge."
8,ETH Zurich,Switzerland,Zurich (Zentrum & Hönggerberg),ETH online portal · Sept 2027,—,30 Apr 2027,Nov–Apr,,https://ethz.ch/en/studies/registration-application/bachelor.html,150,CHF,"₹16,500","4,380","4,400",CHF,4.8,4.8,"ETH Zurich is continental Europe's top-ranked university and one of the world's best for engineering, computer science and natural sciences — with more than 20 Nobel laureates linked to it, including Albert Einstein. Its biggest attraction for international students is value: tuition is only a few thousand Swiss francs a year, a fraction of UK or US fees, for a world-class education. ETH has strong industry ties with companies like Google, which has a major engineering hub in Zurich, and an active startup ecosystem. Zurich itself consistently ranks among the world's most liveable cities. Note that bachelor's programmes are taught in German, so applicants need strong German skills and usually an entrance exam, but the payoff is an elite technical education.",Bachelor's taught in German (C1). Indian Class XII usually needs ETH entrance exam.,"ETH Zurich's mission is to educate the next generation of engineers, scientists and leaders, and to create knowledge and technologies that serve Switzerland and the world. It combines fundamental research with practical application, ensuring that its work drives innovation in industry and society. ETH emphasises a rigorous, research-based education that develops independent, critical thinkers capable of solving complex problems. It values academic freedom, excellence and responsibility towards society and the environment. The university also aims to transfer knowledge to the economy through partnerships and spin-offs, and to engage the public in dialogue about science and technology, building trust and understanding.","ETH Zurich aims to be one of the world's leading universities in science and technology, helping to shape a sustainable future. Its strategic focus areas include climate and energy, health and medical technology, data science and AI, and sustainable materials and manufacturing. ETH envisions strengthening interdisciplinary research, expanding its innovation and entrepreneurship support, and attracting top talent from around the world. It also aims to make its own operations climate-neutral and to embed sustainability into teaching and research. Through partnerships with industry, government and other institutions, ETH wants its discoveries to address global challenges while contributing to Switzerland's prosperity and international reputation."
8,UCL (University College London),UK,"Bloomsbury, London",UCAS · Sept 2027,15 Oct 2026 (Medicine only),~14 Jan 2027,Sept–Jan,,https://www.ucl.ac.uk/prospective-students/undergraduate/application-and-offers,28.5,GBP,"₹3,360","30,000","48,000",GBP,35.4,56.6,"UCL is a top-ten global university in the heart of London, offering one of the broadest ranges of subjects among the UK's elite institutions. It is especially strong in architecture (the Bartlett), medicine, neuroscience, law, economics and education. Founded to open higher education to people of all backgrounds, UCL retains a progressive, diverse culture with students from over 150 countries. Its Bloomsbury campus is surrounded by the British Museum, British Library and leading hospitals, giving students extraordinary resources. London offers unmatched internship and career opportunities across finance, tech, media and policy. UCL's interdisciplinary programmes, such as Arts and Sciences BASc, let students combine fields, and graduates are highly sought after by employers worldwide.",Medicine ~£50k+/yr.,"UCL describes itself as London's global university — a diverse, intellectual community engaged with the wider world and committed to changing it for the better. It was founded in 1826 to open higher education to those excluded elsewhere, regardless of religion, class or later gender, and that commitment to openness remains central. UCL aims to deliver research-based education that develops critical thinkers, and to produce research that addresses real-world problems. It values disruptive, independent thinking and public engagement. Through collaborations across disciplines and with partners in London and globally, UCL seeks to apply its knowledge to improve lives and society.","UCL's strategic vision is to use its breadth, radical thinking and research excellence to address society's toughest challenges. Its priorities include tackling global health, climate change, inequality and the responsible use of technology. UCL aims to deliver an outstanding, inclusive student experience, strengthen interdisciplinary research through its Grand Challenges programme, and expand innovation through its East London campus. It also seeks to deepen partnerships with London's communities, businesses and public institutions, and to make its operations sustainable. The overarching vision is for UCL to be a university that not only generates knowledge, but actively applies it to build a fairer, healthier and more sustainable world."
10,National University of Singapore (NUS),Singapore,"Kent Ridge, Singapore",NUS online portal · Aug 2027,—,~Feb 2027 (varies by qualification),Oct–Feb,,https://www.nus.edu.sg/oam/apply-to-nus,20,SGD,"₹1,360","30,000","40,000",SGD,20.4,27.2,"NUS is Asia's highest-ranked university and a gateway to careers across the region's fastest-growing economies. It offers strong programmes across engineering, computing, business, law, medicine and the sciences, with a flexible curriculum that encourages interdisciplinary study. NUS Overseas Colleges lets students intern at startups in Silicon Valley, Shanghai and elsewhere, and many programmes include global exchange. Singapore is safe, multicultural and English-speaking, with excellent infrastructure and strong job prospects. The MOE Tuition Grant significantly reduces fees for international students in exchange for working in Singapore for three years after graduation — a bond many see as a career advantage. For students wanting a world-class education close to India, NUS is outstanding.",Fee shown is with Tuition Grant (needs 3-yr Singapore work bond). Without grant ~S$40k–60k+.,"NUS's mission is to educate, inspire and transform. It aims to provide a broad-based, interdisciplinary education that nurtures thought leaders and global citizens equipped to thrive in a changing world. NUS pursues research that addresses important challenges facing Singapore, Asia and the world, with strong emphasis on translating discovery into impact. The university values innovation, entrepreneurship and engagement with industry and society. It also seeks to create a vibrant, inclusive community where students develop not only academically but personally, through residential colleges, global experiences and active participation in campus life.","NUS envisions being a leading global university shaping the future, centred in Asia. Its strategic priorities include interdisciplinary education through its College of Humanities and Sciences and College of Design and Engineering, research in areas such as sustainability, health, AI and urban solutions, and strengthening its innovation and enterprise ecosystem. NUS aims to prepare graduates for lifelong learning and careers that may not yet exist, while contributing to Singapore's development as a knowledge economy. It also seeks to deepen partnerships across Asia and globally, positioning itself as a bridge between East and West in education, research and innovation."
11,The University of Hong Kong (HKU),Hong Kong SAR,"Pok Fu Lam, Hong Kong",HKU non-JUPAS portal · Sept 2027,Early round: ~mid-Nov 2026,Main round: ~Jan 2027,Sept–Jan,,https://admissions.hku.hk/apply,450,HKD,"₹5,130","1,82,000","2,00,000",HKD,20.7,22.8,"HKU is Hong Kong's oldest university and one of Asia's best, with English-medium teaching and particular strength in law, medicine, dentistry, business and engineering. Located in a major international financial hub, students have outstanding access to internships with banks, consulting firms and multinationals. HKU combines Western academic traditions with a gateway to mainland China, giving graduates a unique advantage for careers in Asia. Its Common Core curriculum broadens learning across disciplines, and many programmes include exchange options worldwide. Non-local graduates can stay in Hong Kong to seek work under the IANG scheme. With a vibrant city, strong global reputation and rising rankings, HKU is an excellent option for ambitious students targeting Asia-focused careers.",Hostel guaranteed for 1st-yr non-local students (verify).,"HKU's mission is to advance knowledge and educate future leaders through excellent teaching, research and knowledge exchange. It aims to provide a comprehensive education that develops students' intellectual, professional and personal capabilities, preparing them to contribute to Hong Kong, the nation and the world. HKU values academic freedom, integrity and international engagement. Its research spans a wide range of fields, with strength in medicine, public health and the sciences. The university also emphasises knowledge exchange — sharing research with industry, government and the community — so that its work creates tangible benefits for society.","HKU envisions itself as 'Asia's Global University' — a leading international institution that is innovative, impactful and globally connected. Its strategic priorities include internationalisation, interdisciplinarity and innovation, with investment in areas such as AI, data science, public health and sustainability. HKU aims to deepen links with mainland China, particularly the Greater Bay Area, while strengthening partnerships worldwide. It wants to attract top international talent, support entrepreneurship and translate research into impact. The university also seeks to provide a transformative student experience that prepares graduates to be global leaders with a strong sense of social responsibility."
12,Nanyang Technological University (NTU Singapore),Singapore,"Jurong West, Singapore",NTU online portal · Aug 2027,—,~Feb 2027 (varies by qualification),Oct–Feb,,https://www.ntu.edu.sg/admissions/undergraduate,10,SGD,₹680,"28,000","40,000",SGD,19,27.2,"NTU Singapore is one of the world's youngest top-ranked universities and a global leader in engineering, materials science, AI and sustainability research. Its modern, green campus — with award-winning buildings like the Hive — is one of the most beautiful in Asia. NTU has strong industry partnerships with companies such as Rolls-Royce, Alibaba and HP, offering internships and joint research. Programmes like the Renaissance Engineering Programme combine engineering with business and humanities. Singapore offers safety, multicultural life and excellent career prospects, and the MOE Tuition Grant reduces fees in exchange for a three-year work commitment. For students interested in technology, innovation and a future in Asia, NTU is a compelling choice.",Fee with Tuition Grant (work bond applies).,"NTU's mission is to nurture well-rounded graduates who are innovative, future-ready and able to contribute to society. It aims to provide a holistic education that combines deep disciplinary knowledge with interdisciplinary learning, global exposure and character development. NTU pursues research that addresses global challenges, particularly in sustainability, health, technology and education. It values excellence, integrity and collaboration, and emphasises close partnerships with industry and government to translate research into real-world solutions. The university also seeks to create a vibrant residential campus community that supports students' personal growth.","NTU envisions being a great global university founded on science and technology, nurturing leaders through research-intensive and interdisciplinary education for the betterment of humanity. Its NTU 2025 strategic plan focuses on addressing humanity's grand challenges — sustainability, healthy living, technology's impact on society, and responding to the needs of an ageing population. NTU aims to strengthen interdisciplinary research, expand innovation and entrepreneurship, and deepen global partnerships. It also wants to lead in sustainable campus development, making its own operations a living laboratory for green solutions, and to prepare graduates who are adaptable, ethical and ready to lead in a rapidly changing world."
13,Peking University,China,Beijing (Yanyuan),PKU international student portal · Sept 2027,—,~Feb–Mar 2027,Dec–Mar,,https://www.isd.pku.edu.cn/,800,CNY,"₹9,920","26,000","35,000",CNY,3.2,4.3,"Peking University is China's most prestigious comprehensive university and a leader in humanities, social sciences, natural sciences and medicine. Its Beijing campus, Yanyuan, is famed for its traditional architecture and Weiming Lake. Tuition is remarkably low by global standards, and scholarships such as the Chinese Government Scholarship can cover costs entirely. Studying at PKU offers deep insight into China's economy, politics and culture — valuable for careers involving the world's second-largest economy. Its graduates hold influential roles in government, academia and business. International students should note most undergraduate programmes are Chinese-taught, but for those willing to learn Mandarin, PKU provides an elite education and an unmatched network in China.",Most UG programmes Chinese-taught (HSK 5/6 typically required).,"Peking University's mission is to cultivate talented people of integrity, with a sense of social responsibility and a global vision, and to advance knowledge that serves the nation and humanity. Founded in 1898 as China's first modern national university, PKU has a strong tradition of patriotism, progress, democracy and science. It values freedom of thought and inclusive scholarship, encouraging students to think independently and critically. The university aims to produce research of the highest quality across disciplines and to contribute to China's development through policy advice, innovation and public service, while engaging actively with the global academic community.","Peking University aims to become a world-leading university with Chinese characteristics, standing at the forefront of global science, technology and the humanities. Its strategic priorities include strengthening fundamental research, building interdisciplinary platforms in areas such as life sciences, AI, climate and health, and attracting world-class faculty. PKU seeks to deepen international cooperation through partnerships and exchange programmes, while contributing to China's national strategies for innovation and development. It also aims to nurture future leaders who combine expertise with integrity and global awareness, and to share Chinese scholarship and culture with the world."
14,Tsinghua University,China,Beijing (Haidian),Tsinghua international portal · Sept 2027,—,~Feb–Mar 2027,Dec–Mar,,https://www.tsinghua.edu.cn/en/Admissions.htm,800,CNY,"₹9,920","30,000","40,000",CNY,3.7,5,"Tsinghua is often called China's MIT and is among the world's best for engineering, computer science and architecture. Its alumni include many of China's top political and business leaders, and its graduates are highly sought after in tech and industry. Tsinghua's Beijing campus is large and beautiful, with world-class labs and strong links to companies in Zhongguancun, China's Silicon Valley. Tuition is low, and generous scholarships are available for international students. While many programmes are Chinese-taught, a growing number of English options exist. For students interested in engineering, technology and China's rapid innovation economy, Tsinghua offers a rare combination of academic excellence, affordability and career access.",Mostly Chinese-taught; entrance assessment possible.,"Tsinghua's mission, guided by its motto 'Self-discipline and Social Commitment', is to cultivate innovative, high-calibre talent with integrity and a sense of responsibility, and to serve national development through research and innovation. The university emphasises rigorous academics combined with practical application, encouraging students to solve real-world problems. It values both scientific excellence and humanistic learning, aiming to produce graduates who are technically skilled and socially conscious. Tsinghua also seeks to transfer knowledge to industry and society, contributing to economic and technological progress in China and globally.","Tsinghua aims to become a world-class university at the forefront of global higher education. Its strategic direction emphasises interdisciplinary research in areas such as AI, clean energy, integrated circuits, life sciences and global governance. Tsinghua seeks to deepen internationalisation through programmes like Schwarzman Scholars and global partnerships, attracting talent from around the world. It wants to strengthen innovation and entrepreneurship, supporting startups and industry collaboration. The university also aims to nurture leaders who combine expertise with global vision and responsibility, contributing both to China's development and to humanity's shared challenges."
15,University of Pennsylvania,USA,"Philadelphia, Pennsylvania",Common App · Fall 2027,Early Decision (binding): 1 Nov 2026,5 Jan 2027,Aug–Jan,,https://admissions.upenn.edu/how-to-apply,75,USD,"₹6,680","68,000","72,000",USD,60.5,64.1,"Penn is an Ivy League university known for combining academic excellence with practical, career-focused learning. Its Wharton School is the world's leading undergraduate business programme, and Penn is equally strong in engineering, nursing, and arts and sciences. The 'One University' approach lets students take courses across all schools, and dual-degree programmes like M&T (Management and Technology) are hugely popular. Located in Philadelphia, Penn offers a vibrant urban campus with easy access to New York and Washington DC. Its alumni network is powerful in finance, consulting, law and entrepreneurship. For students who want Ivy League prestige plus strong professional outcomes, Penn is an outstanding choice.",Need-aware for international students.,"Penn's mission is rooted in Benjamin Franklin's founding vision of education that combines theory and practice to prepare students for lives of leadership and service. The university aims to advance knowledge through research and teaching, and to apply that knowledge to benefit society. Penn values interdisciplinary learning, encouraging students to draw on expertise across its twelve schools. It is committed to inclusion, access and community engagement, particularly in Philadelphia. The university seeks to produce graduates who are both intellectually rigorous and practically skilled, ready to make meaningful contributions in their chosen fields.","Penn's strategic framework, 'In Principle and Practice', aims to anchor the university's work in addressing major societal challenges. Priorities include advancing health and medicine, tackling climate change, strengthening democracy and civic life, and responsibly harnessing data and technology. Penn seeks to deepen interdisciplinary collaboration, expand access and affordability, and strengthen its partnership with Philadelphia. It also aims to support faculty and students in pursuing bold, impactful research and to cultivate leaders who apply knowledge for the public good. The vision is of a university that combines excellence with a clear sense of purpose."
